Vendored consensus library for ariabc_pg --consensus hotstuff.

libhotstuff  https://github.com/hot-stuff/libhotstuff  34aa50796f201aaab91c4db5aae9d3b7aceddb5c (Apache-2.0)
salticidae   https://github.com/Determinant/salticidae bec7c8fee67ee34d888d2fdc118aefbd65f454c9
secp256k1    https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1 1e6f1f5ad5e7f1e3ef79313ec02023902bf8175c
libuv        https://github.com/libuv/libuv            v1.48.0

Source changes:
- include/hotstuff/crypto.h: SigSecp256k1::serialize no longer uses a static output
  buffer, which corrupted signatures when several replicas share a process
  (hotstuff_engine_test).
- src/consensus.cpp, include/hotstuff/consensus.h: VoteState, do_persist_vote() before
  each vote, restore_vote_state() with no votes until the lock is back.  The voting
  rules themselves are unchanged (hotstuff_vote_state_test).
- include/hotstuff/liveness.h: PMRoundRobinProposer::sync_proposer(), so a replica
  follows the proposer of committed blocks.  on_consensus() restarts a rotation it
  does not end; deleting its timer left the replica rotating forever, ignoring
  impeach().  on_exp_timeout() skips a turn on which on_propose() would throw, as it
  can for a replica that voted above the chain.
Other sources are unmodified. Docs, demos, tests and upstream autotools files are left out;
ariabc_pg/CMakeLists.txt builds these directly, so hosts need no autotools or libuv-dev.
